      "id": "talk:bythebay-20150820-introduction-to-topic-modeling-and-associated-alex-minnaar",
      "type": "Talk",
      "properties": {
        "abstract": "Topic models are a useful way to uncover the hidden thematic structure present in large document collections. In the past, they have been used to aid in searching, browsing and summarization. This talk will deal with the theory behind topic models, how to make them scale to massive document collections, as well as a practical demonstration. In addition, novel methods to evaluate topic models will be presented.\nAlex Minnaar is a Research Engineer at Nitro.",
        "id": "bythebay-20150820-introduction-to-topic-modeling-and-associated-alex-minnaar",
        "order": 1,
        "title": "Introduction to Topic Modeling and Associated Evaluation Techniques"
